decision: changes-requested

Three blockers remain:

- **R16-N46 — high:** Carry planning reads uncommitted module metadata that cleanliness checks exempt. Removing a dependency or lowering criticality can carry a stale result despite the policy committed at HEAD.
- **R16-N47 — medium:** Cancellation clears `material_clean` after material bindings have been retained. Delivery consumers ignore run-level cancellation and can still consume those bindings.
- **R16-N48 — high:** Submodule movement witnessing stops at immediate submodules. Full validation can publish available bindings after a nested submodule moves away and returns.

The existing report-provenance follow-up remains. Details and prior-finding dispositions follow.

Focused CLI tests, delivery/material tests, `go vet ./...` and `go build ./...` passed. Broader runs were interrupted; they are not independent full-matrix passes. The installed CLI predates the subject, while executing the subject CLI failed because its temporary build directory was read-only. Sealed validation evidence is cited separately below. The checkout remains unchanged.

Rules applied: POSE review workflow, backend Go, security, documentation style and delivery evidence. Knowledge governance was consulted; no knowledge artifacts or attestations were written.

